  "review_boundary": [
    "The review checked public module seams, ownership, runtime allowlisting, safe catalog projection, idempotency, optimistic versioning, deadline and entitlement enforcement, additive migration compatibility and official-answer compatibility.",
    "Task delivery, media authorization, answer mutation routes and Progress projection are intentionally deferred to later phases; this gate does not claim those behaviors are shipped.",
    "No live PostgreSQL, email/RabbitMQ or production API smoke test was claimed; 40 existing PostgreSQL integration tests remain environment-skipped."
  ],
  "review_basis": [
    "Practice catalog access uses the public QuestionTypeService and canonical TaskRuntimeProfileRegistry; stored renderer/class/script values are not executed.",
    "Catalog responses expose runtime metadata and readiness only, with no answer or reference-answer fields; unknown and reference-gap entries are blocked explicitly rather than silently remapped.",
    "Session mutations are student-owned, organization-bound and guarded by live entitlement, server deadline, optimistic version and durable operation idempotency records.",
    "Start insert races are isolated in a REQUIRES_NEW persistence boundary so a losing idempotency-key race can read the committed winner safely.",
    "Practice sessions and attempt links are additive and explicitly PRACTICE-sourced; official attempt submit callers remain source-compatible and confidence is optional.",
    "Feature-flagged student controllers and the existing module-structure checks prevent an unconfigured rollout from exposing the new boundary."
  ],
